-- title:
--   Frobenius automorphism of K(μ_{q^N-1})/K over a q-adic field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $K$ be an intermediate field of the extension $\mathbb{Q}_q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ (the algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl q`) which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, and let $N$ be a natural number with $N > 0$. Write $L_N$ for the intermediate field `IntermediateField.adjoin K {ζ | ζ ^ (q ^ N - 1) = 1}` obtained by adjoining to $K$ all elements of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ satisfying $\zeta^{q^N-1} = 1$, and let `Rw q K` be the valuation subring of $K$ obtained by pulling back, along $K \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$, the valuation subring attached to the canonical valuation of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ with values in $\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ (that is, the ring of integers of $K$). The assertion is that there exist a $K$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $L_N$ and a natural number $a$ such that $a > 0$, the residue field of `Rw q K` has cardinality exactly $q^a$ (as a `Nat.card`), and for every $\zeta \in L_N$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ satisfies $\zeta^{q^N-1} = 1$ one has $\varphi(\zeta) = \zeta^{q^a}$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$. Nothing is claimed about $\varphi$ generating the Galois group.
--
--   This is the existence half of the standard description of the unramified layer $K(\mu_{q^N-1})/K$ of a finite extension $K$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$: a $K$-automorphism acting on the $(q^N-1)$-st roots of unity by raising to the power $\#\kappa_K = q^a$, i.e. a Frobenius. It feeds the identification of $\mathrm{Gal}(K(\mu_{q^N-1})/K)$ as cyclic generated by this automorphism, via [`IntermediateField.exists_generator_frobenius_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_padic`](thm.html#IntermediateField.exists_generator_frobenius_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_padic) and [`IntermediateField.finrank_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_padic_eq_orderOf`](thm.html#IntermediateField.finrank_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_padic_eq_orderOf), and the power-map statement [`PadicAlgCl.exists_algEquiv_apply_eq_pow_of_pow_eq_one`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.exists_algEquiv_apply_eq_pow_of_pow_eq_one).
